# UI Tokens — Bardak

## Colors & Text Styles

Access ONLY through context extensions. Never use raw values in UI code.

```dart
// ✅
Container(color: context.colors.secondary)
Text('Hello', style: context.typography.regular38)

// ❌
Container(color: const Color(0xFF7E2210))
Text('Hello', style: const TextStyle(fontSize: 38))
```

Context extensions are defined in `lib/utils/extensions/context_extension.dart`:

```dart
context.colors      // → AppColors (scheme-aware)
context.typography  // → AppTextStyles (singleton)
context.appTheme    // → AppThemeData
```

## Theme Selection

The active color scheme is driven by `ThemesBloc`. `AppThemeProvider` (an `InheritedWidget`)
wraps the app in `main.dart` and re-builds when the scheme changes.
Do NOT read scheme state directly in widgets — use `context.colors`.

## Assets

Use `flutter_gen` generated accessors only. Run code gen after adding assets to `pubspec.yaml`.

```dart
// ✅
Assets.images.logo.image()
Assets.images.icon.svg()

// ❌
Image.asset('assets/images/logo.png')
SvgPicture.asset('assets/icons/icon.svg')
```

## Widget Rules

- Use `const` constructors for all stateless/immutable widgets.
- Prefer private widget classes (`_ScoreCard`) over `_buildScoreCard()` methods.
- Use `BlocSelector` for partial rebuilds — avoid rebuilding on unrelated state changes.
- Remote images MUST use `CachedNetworkImage` with an `errorBuilder`.

```dart
// ✅ partial rebuild
BlocSelector<SettingsBloc, SettingsState, bool>(
  selector: (state) => state.gameSettings.soundEnabled,
  builder: (context, soundEnabled) => SoundToggle(enabled: soundEnabled),
)
```

## Game UI Specifics

- Win animations: use `confetti` package.
- Active/selected item highlight: use `gradient_borders` package.
- Dynamic board layouts: use `LayoutBuilder`.
